    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": [
        "Each beat must land **16 to 28 game ticks** after the one before, about a second. A strike within 4 ticks of the last is ignored, and a wrong beat thuds and resets the count. Wait too long and a half-played rhythm fades away.",
        "Each drum answers once per **twenty minutes of real time**, and never while its keeper is already awake; it tells you how many minutes are left. If The Unsung resets because everyone left, the drum can be played again at once.",
        "A comparator reads the drum: **3** per beat counted, and a flash of **15** when a rhythm completes."
      ],
      "title": "The rhythm, exactly"
    },
    {
      "type": "recipe",
      "item": "tribalpower:silent_drum",
      "text": "A drum you build yourself works the same way: The Unsung rises wherever it stands."
